{% comment %}
  LOCAL ADDITION -- not an override of anything in the gem.

  al_folio_core's templates check for optional hook includes and render them if the
  file exists (the same pattern `_layouts/bib.liquid` uses for
  `_includes/hook/bib.liquid`). This file is the <head> equivalent: it lets a page
  add tags to the document head without copying the gem's whole head template into
  this repo, which is not possible here anyway since there is no Ruby on this
  machine to read the gem from (CLAUDE.md rule 3).

  Its only job today is `noindex`. A page with

    noindex: true

  in its front matter asks search engines not to index it. That is one of the three
  parts of the unlisted-page pattern in CLAUDE.md §8; the other two, `nav: false`
  and `sitemap: false`, are handled by the navbar and by jekyll-sitemap and need no
  template support. See _pages/talks.md.

  VERIFY BEFORE RELYING ON IT. Whether the gem actually calls a head hook is
  unconfirmed -- it could not be checked locally without the gem installed. After
  the first deploy, run:

    curl -s https://gafap.github.io/talks/ | grep -c noindex   # expect 1
    curl -s https://gafap.github.io/         | grep -c noindex   # expect 0

  If the first returns 0 the hook is not wired up in this gem version, and the
  noindex has to come from somewhere else. Note this matters only once robots.txt
  stops blocking the whole site (CLAUDE.md §8) -- until then nothing is indexed
  regardless.
{% endcomment %}

{% if page.noindex %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
{% endif %}
